#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.8` `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)` (YMD 2025 3 1) 730
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.8` `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)` (YMD 2025 3 1) 731
-- The terms themselves.
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in calendar months` `the offence of contravening a requirement under Article 26(1) or (4)` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in calendar months` `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in calendar months` `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `Art 29(1) the penalty provided for the offence`'s `imprisonment up to, in months` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `Art 29(1) the penalty provided for the offence`'s `fine` EQUALS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 29(1) the maximum fine` BECAUSE "Article 29(1) states no maximum for the fine"

§ `Tests of the private readings of Article 26, called directly`

-- Each reading of each fork of Article 26 is its own function, with its own test; the public functions above are tested against them by the fork assertions.

#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the entity is or was a registered charity` `T26 a registered charity in the general section`
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the entity is or was a registered charity` `T26 an applicant that was formerly a registered charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the entity is or was a registered charity` `T26 an applicant that was never registered`

-- F8.17: reading A takes a governor of an entity registered at any time, reading B only a governor while the entity was registered.
#ASSERT `Art 26(2)(b) reading A: a governor or former governor of an entity registered at any time` `T26 a governor of an entity before it was registered`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2)(b) reading B: a governor while the entity was registered` `T26 a governor of an entity before it was registered`
#ASSERT `Art 26(2)(b) reading B: a governor while the entity was registered` `T26 a governor of a registered charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2)(b) reading A: a governor or former governor of an entity registered at any time` `T26 a governor of an applicant that was never registered`

-- F8.7: the two counts of 14 days from 1 June 2026, and a date.
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) reading A: the last day allowed by the notice, the day of service not counted` `T26 a period of fourteen days` `T26 the first of June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) reading B: the last day allowed by the notice, the day of service counted` `T26 a period of fourteen days` `T26 the first of June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 14
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) reading A: the last day allowed by the notice, the day of service not counted` `T26 a date fixed by the notice, the twentieth of June 2026` `T26 the first of June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 20
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) reading B: the last day allowed by the notice, the day of service counted` `T26 a date fixed by the notice, the twentieth of June 2026` `T26 the first of June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 20

-- F8.19: the two charities.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now` `T26 an employee of a formerly registered entity`
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now or formerly` `T26 an employee of a formerly registered entity`
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now` `T26 an employee of a charity registered now`
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now or formerly` `T26 an employee of a charity registered now`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now` `T26 an employee who appears to hold no relevant information`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(4)(a) the person appears to be a governor or employee of a charity registered now or formerly` `T26 a stranger who holds relevant information`

-- F8.10: the anniversary of a day; the third of the three years that differ is 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(a) the anniversary of the day the year starts` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2029 2 28
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(a) the anniversary of the day the year starts` `the interpretation with the other reading of F8.10` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(a) the anniversary of the day the year starts` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 2 20) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 20

-- 26(5)(b): once proceedings were commenced within the year, the later of the year's end and their conclusion.
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(b) the end of the retention when proceedings were commenced within the year` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 retention, proceedings commenced and concluded within the year` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` (YMD 2027 2 20)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(b) the end of the retention when proceedings were commenced within the year` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 retention, proceedings concluded after the year` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` (YMD 2027 5 15)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(b) the end of the retention when proceedings were commenced within the year` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 retention, proceedings commenced on the anniversary` EQUALS `retention is permitted until proceedings conclude, and they have not concluded`

